  "narrative": {
    "intro": "West Virginia has received $1.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 4,446 awards, with an average award size of $377K. Obligations fell 10.7% year over year. Annual totals show a rise from $1.5B in FY21 and FY22 to a peak of $2B in FY24, then a decline to $1.9B in FY25 and $1.7B in FY26. The largest buyers in FY2026 to date are the Department of Defense, the Department of Energy, and the Department of Veterans Affairs. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences, Other Computer Related Services, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction are the top industry categories by obligations. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP, LEIDOS, INC., and MAVERIS LLC are the top vendors by obligations in the state. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date totals, not final year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal spending in West Virginia?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $344M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy obligated $343M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $308M. The Department of Justice, the Department of the Treasury, and the Department of Homeland Security follow with $234M, $142M, and $109M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries win the most federal work in West Virginia?",
        "body": "NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP obligated $199M and LEIDOS, INC. obligated $159M in FY2026 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $192M and Other Computer Related Services accounted for $179M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $158M."
      }
    ]
  },
